The debt models' oracle cases (contract v29; W12.3; ENG1 §4; ruling 565),
read by src/bonds/oracle.rs and src/bonds/tests.rs; never edited by hand.

- platform-v29-packages.json: the five debt templates' calculation packages
  as open-meridian/meridian-platform publishes them, at c701ce6
  (platform_site/domain/data/templates-v29.json, its `calculation_package`
  per template): Treasury's published auction results (Fiscal Data's
  auctions_query) under 31 CFR 356 Appendix B, a bill's discount, MSRB Rule
  G-33's 30/360 accrual, a pool's and a class's month, a CD's accrual and a
  TBA's market value in percent of par. Every case is answered exactly.
- treasury-curve.json: Treasury's daily par yield curve for 2026-10-01 and
  2026-10-16 and the Board's zero curve (feds200628, SVENY01 to SVENY30) for
  the same dates, as plugin-us-treasury and plugin-fed-board recorded them
  (src/us_treasury/responses/par-202610.csv.gz,
  src/fed_board/responses/feds200628.csv.gz); and QuantLib 1.40's
  PiecewiseConvexMonotoneForward fitted to the par yields through
  FixedRateBondHelpers at par (semi-annual, ActualActual Bond, Backward,
  unadjusted), Actual365Fixed, its continuous zero rates.
- bond-functions.json: QuantLib 1.40's BondFunctions (bondYield, duration
  Macaulay and Modified, convexity, basisPointValue, accruedAmount and
  zSpread over the curve above) for four fixed-rate bonds settled
  2026-10-19 for a close on 2026-10-16.

QuantLib is a test oracle only: its answers are pinned here from the pinned
release (the SDK's, 1.40), never a dependency of this crate or the image.
